        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This principle of short before long is, in fact, one of the unifying principles of a clear prose style:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                117,
                772,
                168
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
            "global_group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    168.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    168.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- It applies to the subject-verb sequence of individual sentences: short subjects better introduce longer, more complex elements that follow.",
            "block_bbox": [
                117,
                181,
                770,
                232
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    117.0,
                    181.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    181.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    232.0
                ],
                [
                    117.0,
                    232.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- It is consistent with the principle of old before new: old information is usually objectively shorter than new information, but it is “psychologically” shorter as well.",
            "block_bbox": [
                118,
                239,
                771,
                314
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    118.0,
                    239.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    239.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    314.0
                ],
                [
                    118.0,
                    314.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- It governs the order of logical elements of a long sentence: a sentence is clearer when it begins with a short statement of its point and then adds the longer and more complex explanatory or supporting information.",
            "block_bbox": [
                117,
                323,
                771,
                400
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    117.0,
                    323.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    323.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    400.0
                ],
                [
                    117.0,
                    400.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- It applies again here in balanced coordination: put shorter elements before longer ones.",
            "block_bbox": [
                117,
                407,
                771,
                457
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
